helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150791				0	pt-BR	Duplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3151211				0	pt-BR	Parâmetros:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3151041				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>Number:\</emph\> qualquer expressão numérica para a qual você deseje calcular o logaritmo natural.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3150869				0	pt-BR	O logaritmo natural é o logaritmo de base e, que é uma constante com um valor aproximado de 2,718282...				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3153968				0	pt-BR	Para calcular logaritmos de qualquer base (n) para qualquer número (x), divida o logaritmo natural de x pelo logaritmo natural de n, desta forma:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3145420				0	pt-BR	Log n(x) = Log(x) / Log(n)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155131				0	pt-BR	Exemplo:				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3152463				0	pt-BR	Sub ExampleLogExp				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3145750				0	pt-BR	Dim a as Double				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3151116				0	pt-BR	Dim const b1=12.345e12				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3146985				0	pt-BR	Dim const b2=1.345e34				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3148616				0	pt-BR	a=Exp( Log(b1)+Log(b2) )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\sbasic\shared\03080202.xhp	0	help	par_id3149262				0	pt-BR	MsgBox "" & a & chr(13) & (b1*b2) ,0,"Multiplicação pela função logarítmo"				20200411 15:09:53
