helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_import_export_limitations.xhp	0	help	par_id0811200801491971				0	pt-BR	Um exemplo das diferenças entre o Calc e o Excel é o tratamento de valores booleanos. Entre VERDADEIRO nas células A1 e A2.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_import_export_limitations.xhp	0	help	par_id0811200801491973				0	pt-BR	No Calc, a fórmula =A1+A2 retorna o valor 2, e a fórmula =SOMA(A1;A2) retorna 2. 				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_import_export_limitations.xhp	0	help	par_id0811200801491972				0	pt-BR	No Excel, a fórmula =A1+A2 retorna 2, mas a fórmula =SOMA(A1,A2) retorna 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\shared\guide\ms_import_export_limitations.xhp	0	help	par_id3150439				0	pt-BR	For a detailed overview about converting documents to and from Microsoft Office format, see the \<link href=\"https://wiki.openoffice.org/wiki/Documentation/OOoAuthors_User_Manual/Migration_Guide\"\>Migration Guide\</link\>.				20200411 15:09:53
