helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155260				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>Valor1; Valor2, ..., Valor30\</emph\> são valores ou intervalos. Os textos tem valor 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149504				0	pt-BR	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150864				0	pt-BR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MÉDIAA(A1:A50)\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148754K1				0	pt-BR	\<bookmark_value\>AVERAGEIF function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148754K1				0	pt-BR	AVERAGEIF				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145138K1				0	pt-BR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MITTELWERTB\"\>Average the values of cells in a range that meet a criteria.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153326K1				0	pt-BR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149734K1				0	pt-BR	AVERAGEIF( Reference R ; Criterion C [ ; Reference A ] )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155260K1				0	pt-BR	 If reference A is omitted, averages the values of cells in the reference range R that meet the Criterion C. If reference A is given, averages the values of cells of a range that is constructed using the top left cell of reference A and applying the dimensions, shape and size, of reference R.  Does not accept constant values as reference parameters.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145139K1				0	pt-BR	If no cell in range R matches the Criterion C, an Error is returned. If no Numbers are in the range to be averaged, an Error is returned.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149504K1				0	pt-BR	Examples				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150864K1				0	pt-BR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=AVERAGEIF(A1:A50;">"0)\</item\>will return the average of A1:A50 of all positive values in the range.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148754K2				0	pt-BR	\<bookmark_value\>AVERAGEIFS function\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148754K2				0	pt-BR	AVERAGEIFS				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145138K2				0	pt-BR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MITTELWERTC\"\>Average the values of cells that meet multiple criteria in multiple ranges.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153326K2				0	pt-BR	Syntax				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149734K2				0	pt-BR	AVERAGEIFS( Reference A ; Reference R1 ; Criterion C1 [ ; Reference R2 ; Criterion C2 ]... )				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155260K2				0	pt-BR	Averages the values of cells in the reference range A that meet the Criterion C1 in the reference range R1 and the Criterion C2 in the reference range R2, and so on.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145139K2				0	pt-BR	All reference ranges shall have the same dimension and size, else an Error is returned. A logical AND is applied between each array result of each selection; a cell of reference range A is evaluated only if the same position in each array is the result of a Criterion match. If no numbers are in the result set to be averaged, an Error is returned.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149504K2				0	pt-BR	Example				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150864K2				0	pt-BR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=AVERAGEIFS(A1:A50;B1:B25;">"0)\</item\>+will return the average of A1:A50 if all cells in the range B1 to B25 are greater than 0.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153933				0	pt-BR	\<bookmark_value\>função MODO\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>valor mais comum\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153933				0	pt-BR	MODO				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153085				0	pt-BR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_MODALWERT\"\>Retorna o valor mais comum em um conjunto de dados.\</ahelp\> Se houver vários valores com a mesma frequência, o menor valor será retornado. Um erro ocorre quando um valor não aparece duas vezes.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153003				0	pt-BR	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155950				0	pt-BR	MODO(Número1; Número2; ...; Número30)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150337				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>Número1; Número2;...Número30\</emph\> são valores numéricos ou intervalos.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153571				0	pt-BR	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153733				0	pt-BR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=MODO(A1:A50)\</item\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3149879				0	pt-BR	\<bookmark_value\>função DIST.BIN.NEG\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>distribuição binomial negativa\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149879				0	pt-BR	DIST.BIN.NEG				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155437				0	pt-BR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_NEGBINOMVERT\"\>Retorna a distribuição binomial negativa.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3145351				0	pt-BR	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150935				0	pt-BR	DIST.BIN.NEG(X; R; SP)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153044				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>X\</emph\> representa o valor retornado para testes que não tiveram êxito.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151018				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>R\</emph\> representa o valor retornado para sucessos.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148878				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>PS\</emph\> é a probabilidade de sucesso de uma tentativa.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3149539				0	pt-BR	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148770				0	pt-BR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DIST.BIN.NEG(1;1;0,5)\</item\> retorna 0,25.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3155516				0	pt-BR	\<bookmark_value\>função INV.NORM\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>distribuição normal;inverso de\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155516				0	pt-BR	INV.NORM				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154634				0	pt-BR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_NORMINV\"\>Retorna o inverso da distribuição acumulada normal.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153227				0	pt-BR	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147534				0	pt-BR	INV.NORM(Número; Média; DesvPad)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154950				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>Número\</emph\> representa o valor de probabilidade utilizado para determinar a distribuição normal inversa.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150690				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>Média\</emph\> representa o valor da média na distribuição normal.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148594				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>DesvPad\</emph\> representa o desvio padrão da distribuição normal.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155822				0	pt-BR	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153921				0	pt-BR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=INV.NORM(0,9;63;5)\</item\> retorna 69,41. Se a média dos ovos é de 63 gramas com desvio padrão de 5, então há 90% de chances que os ovos não pesarão mais de 69,41 gramas.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153722				0	pt-BR	\<bookmark_value\>função DIST.NORM\</bookmark_value\>\<bookmark_value\>função de densidade\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153722				0	pt-BR	DIST.NORM				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150386				0	pt-BR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_NORMVERT\"\>Retorna a função de densidade ou a distribuição acumulada normal.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3083282				0	pt-BR	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150613				0	pt-BR	DIST.NORM(Número; Média; DesvPad; C)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149820				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>Número\</emph\> é o valor da distribuição para calcular a distribuição normal.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3146063				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>Média\</emph\> é o valor da média da distribuição.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3156295				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>DesvPad\</emph\> é o desvio padrão da distribuição.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3145080				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>C\</emph\> é opcional. \<emph\>C\</emph\> = 0 calcula a função densidade; \<emph\>C\</emph\> = 1 calcula a distribuição.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152972				0	pt-BR	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149283				0	pt-BR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DIST.NORM(70;63;5;0)\</item\> retorna 0.03.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149448				0	pt-BR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=DIST.NORM(70;63;5;1)\</item\> retorna 0.92.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152934				0	pt-BR	\<bookmark_value\>função PEARSON\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152934				0	pt-BR	PEARSON				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153216				0	pt-BR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_PEARSON\"\>Retorna o coeficiente de correlação r do momento do produto Pearson.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147081				0	pt-BR	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3156133				0	pt-BR	PEARSON(Dados1; Dados2)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151272				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>Dados1\</emph\> representa a matriz do primeiro conjunto de dados.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153279				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>Dados2\</emph\> representa a matriz do segundo conjunto de dados.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147567				0	pt-BR	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151187				0	pt-BR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PEARSON(A1:A30;B1:B30)\</item\> retorna o coeficiente de correlação de Pearson para dois conjuntos de dados.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3152806				0	pt-BR	\<bookmark_value\>função FI\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3152806				0	pt-BR	FI				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150254				0	pt-BR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_PHI\"\>Retorna os valores da função de distribuição para uma distribuição normal padrão.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154748				0	pt-BR	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149976				0	pt-BR	FI(Número)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3156108				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>Número\</emph\> representa o argumento para a distribuição normal padrão.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153621				0	pt-BR	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3155849				0	pt-BR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=FI(2,25) \</item\>= 0,03				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3143236				0	pt-BR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=FI(-2,25)\</item\> = 0,03				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149286				0	pt-BR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=FI(0)\</item\> = 0,4				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153985				0	pt-BR	\<bookmark_value\>função POISSON\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153985				0	pt-BR	POISSON				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154298				0	pt-BR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_POISSON\"\>Retorna a distribuição de Poisson.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159183				0	pt-BR	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3146093				0	pt-BR	POISSON(Número; Média; C)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147253				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>Número\</emph\> representa o valor que serve de base para o cálculo da distribuição de Poisson.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3151177				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>Média\</emph\> representa o valor do meio da distribuição de Poisson.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149200				0	pt-BR	            \<emph\>C\</emph\> (opcional) = 0 ou Falso calcula a função densidade; \<emph\>C\</emph\> = 1 ou Verdadeiro calcula a distribuição. Se omitido, o valor padrão Verdadeiro será inserido ao salvar o documento, para melhor compatibilidade com outros programas e versões antigas do %PRODUCTNAME.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3159347				0	pt-BR	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3150113				0	pt-BR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=POISSON(60;50;1)\</item\> retorna 0,93.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3153100				0	pt-BR	\<bookmark_value\>função PERCENTIL\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3153100				0	pt-BR	PERCENTIL				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154940				0	pt-BR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_QUANTIL\"\>Retorna o alfa-percentil dos valores dos dados em uma matriz.\</ahelp\> Um percentil retorna o valor de escala para uma série de dados que vai do menor (Alfa=0) ao maior valor (Alfa=1) de uma série de dados. Para \<item type=\"literal\"\>Alfa\</item\> = 25%, o percentil significa o quartil; \<item type=\"literal\"\>Alfa\</item\> = 50% é a MED.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3150531				0	pt-BR	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148813				0	pt-BR	PERCENTIL(Dados; Alfa)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153054				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>Dados\</emph\> representa a matriz dos dados.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154212				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>Alfa\</emph\> representa a porcentagem da escala entre 0 e 1.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3154290				0	pt-BR	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3159147				0	pt-BR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=PERCENTIL(A1:A50;0,1)\</item\> representa o valor no conjunto de dados, que iguala 10% da escala total dos dados em A1:A50.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3148807				0	pt-BR	\<bookmark_value\>função ORDEM.PERCENTUAL\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3148807				0	pt-BR	ORDEM.PERCENTUAL				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3153573				0	pt-BR	\<ahelp hid=\"HID_FUNC_QUANTILSRANG\"\>Retorna a ordem percentual de um valor em uma amostra.\</ahelp\>				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3147512				0	pt-BR	Sintaxe				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3147238				0	pt-BR	ORDEM.PERCENTUAL(Dados; Valor)				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3154266				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>Dados\</emph\> representa a matriz de dados em uma amostra.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3148475				0	pt-BR	\<emph\>Valor\</emph\> representa o valor cuja ordem percentil será determinada.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	hd_id3155364				0	pt-BR	Exemplo				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	par_id3149163				0	pt-BR	\<item type=\"input\"\>=ORDEM.PERCENTUAL(A1:A50;50)\</item\> retorna a ordem percentual do valor 50 a partir do intervalo total de valores em A1:A50. Se 50 não estiver dentro do intervalo total, aparecerá uma mensagem de erro.				20200411 15:09:53
helpcontent2	source\text\scalc\01\04060184.xhp	0	help	bm_id3166442				0	pt-BR	\<bookmark_value\>função QUARTIL\</bookmark_value\>				20200411 15:09:53
